<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Page Not Found</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <style>
    * {
      line-height: 1.2;
      margin: 0;
    }

    html {
      color: #000;
      display: table;
      font-family: sans-serif;
      height: 100%;
      text-align: left;
      width: 100%;
	  margin-top: 10px;
	  margin-left: 10px;
    }

    body {
      display: table-cell;
      vertical-align: top;
      margin: 2em auto;
    }

    h1 {
      color: #000;
      font-size: 2em;
      font-weight: 400;
    }

    p {
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    @media only screen and (max-width: 280px) {
	
	  html {
	    text-align: center;
	  }
	  
	  body {
	    vertical-align: middle;
	  }

      body,
      p {
        width: 95%;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 1.5em;
        margin: 0 0 0.3em;
      }

    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <img src="https://store.ctr-electronics.com/content/logo/ctre_logo_onWhite_cropped.png" alt="CTR Electronics Logo" width="230">
  <p></br></p>
  <h1>Page Not Found</h1>
  <p></br>Sorry, but the page you were trying to view does not exist.</br> </br>
     This can happen if you attempt to view a directory.</br>This repository only supports direct file access with the fully-qualified URL.</br> </br>
	 If you're attempting to download a file or binary artifact, be sure to put the full path (including filename) into the browser.</p>
</body>

</html>
<!-- IE needs 512+ bytes: https://docs.microsoft.com/archive/blogs/ieinternals/friendly-http-error-pages -->